  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Friday)\nIssued at 1252 PM MDT Sat Aug 8 2026\n\nMonday through Wednesday sees a subtle trend of lowering \ntemperatures and an increase in monsoonal moisture as the center of \nthe high slides over NM. Daily rounds of afternoon thunderstorms \nfavoring development over the high terrain with slow motions over \nnearby highlands and lower elevations will remain the rule. By \nThursday, the monsoon high will recenter itself more as a westerly \nappendage of the Bermuda high over TX. This will continue the trend \nof cooler more seasonally average temperatures alongside an uptick \nin monsoonal moisture advecting northward from the Gulf of CA into \nthe Desert Southwest. PWs trends upwards to the 1.00\" to 1.20\" mark, \nnearing or surpassing the 90th percentile for mid-August. This will \nyield healthier and more widespread crops of afternoon thunderstorms \ncapable of producing locally heavy rainfall across western, central, \nand northern NM. Poorly drained areas or recent burn scars will have \na higher risk of flash flooding during this timeframe.",
